{"name":"Feldspar","hex":"#d19275","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"feldspar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a large group of rock-forming aluminosilicate minerals containing potassium, sodium, or calcium that, together, make up about 60% of the Earth's outer crust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feldspar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Feldspar","blocks":[{"text":"Feldspar is a group of rock-forming aluminium tectosilicate minerals, also containing other cations such as sodium, calcium, potassium, or barium. The most common members of the feldspar group are the plagioclase (sodium-calcium) feldspars and the alkali (potassium-sodium) feldspars. Feldspars make up about 60% of the Earth's crust and 41% of the Earth's continental crust by weight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Feldspar_diversity.png/330px-Feldspar_diversity.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feldspar"},{"title":"Feldspar (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Feldspar is an album by saxophonist and composer Matana Roberts, electric guitarist Sam Shalabi, and double bassist Nicolas Caloia. Consisting of seven improvised tracks named after minerals, it was recorded on December 8, 2011, at Studio Hotel2Tango in Montreal, Canada, and was released in 2014 by the Canadian Tour de Bras label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/61/Roberts_Shalabi_Caloia_Feldspar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feldspar_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Anorthite_crankshaft.png/120px-Anorthite_crankshaft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Anorthite_crankshaft.png/250px-Anorthite_crankshaft.png?utm_source=en.wikipe